# Independent Vault bundle integrity review

This read-only review authenticates the frozen ready bundle, its public copy list, the five accepted runtime files, and the exact 82-artifact final independent review. No candidate tests, original application executions, browser operations, or measurements are performed.

Public content checks reject MZ/PK file prefixes, exact original archive or executable/library identities, and embedded complete original executable/library/archive payloads. These are finite publication-carrier checks; they do not claim a universal security audit.

The stage directory contains 1,442 preserved artifacts plus its manifest and freeze metadata, for 1,444 public paths. Twelve full original source ZIP carriers are bundle-local, outside the copy list. Their identities plus the 1,442 public stage artifact identities match the original 1,454-artifact stage manifest, including duplicate multiplicities.

The initial audit incorrectly applied the 1,442 artifact count to all stage directory paths. Its exact source and reproduced raw failure are preserved under `failures/stage-count-v1`. The corrected audit preserves that failure as a harness accounting error. The frozen `INTEGRATION.md` also says four local archive copies; the authenticated count is twelve (four named historical copies plus eight acquisition descendants). Root has retained that prose historically and will correct current documentation without changing frozen bytes.

`review-validation.json` states the accepted evidence and limits. `review-manifest.json` binds every review artifact except itself and `freeze.json`; `freeze.json` binds the receipt and manifest. Production and bundle files are not modified.
